    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297">

                <pb facs="0273" n="259" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/2422: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Briggs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-09T18:00:00-05:00">April 9, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>184. Department’s 181, April 8, 10 p.m. The Prime Minister<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d297-f1"/> enthusiastically endorses the establishment of patrols
                    based on San <pb facs="0274" n="260" xml:id="pg260"/> Julián “or at any other
                    point in Cuba from which we desire to operate”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Briggs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d297-f1" n="19" xml:id="d297-f1-content">
